      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GINGER GREEN (1) sat handy first-up over 1400m and was strong to the line, only edged out by 0.9L in a terrific return. Out in trip now is a big tick and he should get every chance from the inside draw. He loves this track and trip and after an impressive return, he can land the knockout blow. RIGHT TO SILENCE (8) missed narrowly two back in a good form race before a 2.6L defeat most recently, both over 1400m. She now rises to the mile for just the second time but it doesn't look an issue on what we've seen from her recently. She'll end up in the second half of the field most likely, but she rates highly on her recent efforts and can't be discounted. STRAPPING PROPHET (3) is better than she showed last time out on the heavy deck, with her runs here prior stacking right up. Can bounce back in a big way. KELVINATER (5) was too good from the front last time and can repeat the dose. OUR ROCKY BAY (2) won't be far away with his formlines tying in.",
